{{!
    @template mod_examcheck/seat_assign

    Seat assignment page: the assignment count, the auto-assign trigger, and the seat
    dynamic table. Each row of the table server-renders a select holding only the
    currently assigned student; the JS enhances it into an AJAX autocomplete, saves
    changes instantly, and re-enhances every row after the table body reloads on sort
    or paging.

    The two counts on the root let the JS size the auto-assign confirmation without a
    roundtrip, and keep the count line live: assigning a student consumes one free seat
    and one unseated student, unassigning returns one of each.

    Never let two closing braces meet inside a comment such as this one. Mustache closes
    a comment at the first pair it meets, and the rest of the block would then be rendered
    as literal text. Keep the example context flat, with no nested objects.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-region="examcheck-seat-assign" - the page root, carries the cmid and the counts
    * data-region="examcheck-seat-count" - the seat and student count text
    * data-region="examcheck-autoassign" - wraps the trigger, hidden when nothing to assign
    * data-action="examcheck-autoassign" - the trigger itself

    Context variables required for this template:
    * cmid - course module id
    * assignedcount - number of assigned seats
    * seatcount - total number of seats
    * freeseats - number of seats with no student
    * rostercount - reachable roster students, seated or not
    * studentsassigned - reachable roster students who have a seat
    * unseatedstudents - reachable roster students with no seat
    * canautoassign - whether there is at least one free seat and one unseated student
    * table - the rendered seat_assign dynamic table

    Example context (json):
    {
        "cmid": 12,
        "assignedcount": 1,
        "seatcount": 2,
        "freeseats": 1,
        "rostercount": 4,
        "studentsassigned": 1,
        "unseatedstudents": 3,
        "canautoassign": true,
        "table": "<table class=\"generaltable\"><tbody><tr><td>A1</td></tr></tbody></table>"
    }
}}
<div data-region="examcheck-seat-assign"
     data-cmid="{{cmid}}"
     data-seatcount="{{seatcount}}"
     data-freeseats="{{freeseats}}"
     data-rostercount="{{rostercount}}"
     data-unseatedstudents="{{unseatedstudents}}">
    <p class="text-muted">
        <span data-region="examcheck-seat-count">
            {{#str}}
                seatandstudentcount, mod_examcheck,
                { "seats": {{assignedcount}}, "seatstotal": {{seatcount}},
                  "students": {{studentsassigned}}, "studentstotal": {{rostercount}} }
            {{/str}}
        </span>
        <span data-region="examcheck-autoassign" class="{{^canautoassign}}d-none{{/canautoassign}}">
            &ndash;
            <button type="button"
                    class="btn btn-link p-0 align-baseline"
                    data-action="examcheck-autoassign">
                {{#str}} autoassign, mod_examcheck {{/str}}
            </button>
        </span>
    </p>
    {{{table}}}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['mod_examcheck/seat_assign'], function(SeatAssign) {
    SeatAssign.init({{cmid}});
});
{{/js}}
